# No real robot runs

**Never** start, trigger, or command a real robot motion/test run unless the user explicitly asks for that specific run in the current message.

## Forbidden without explicit user ask

- `POST /modes/lightsout/runs`, `POST /modes/mock/runs`, or any other run-start API against a live cell
- Calling ROS services that start trees (`bt_start_lightsout`, `bt_start_webhook_weightment`, MoveTo / scoop / pour actions)
- “Smoke tests”, “validation runs”, or deploy acceptance that move the arm, scoop, or pour
- Assuming “validate on Pi” or a plan checklist implies permission to run hardware

## Allowed without asking

- Read-only checks: HTTP GETs, container status, logs, topic echo, image/tag verification
- Unit/integration tests that do not talk to the live robot
- Building, pushing, deploying software images

## If a plan or todo says “smoke run on the robot”

Stop and ask the user. Do not start the run yourself.
